{
  "description": "Stock movement (RPT-13, W2-02 plan): one item's opening, its movements by bucket and its closing, in quantity (thousandths) and value. Buckets are signed (in +, out −), so opening + every bucket = closing. A sale's line out is a sale and one in is a return; a void undoes its bill (stock back undoes a sale, stock out undoes a return); a transfer is out of one location and into another. An unknown source is refused.",
